[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat dumpcpu - dumps cpu stats
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat groupname[+] - toggles displaying stats group, + enables hierarchical display
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat hier -group=groupname [-sortby=name] [-maxhistoryframes=60] [-reset] [-maxdepth=4]
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]	- groupname is a stat group like initviews or statsystem
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]	- sortby can be name (by stat FName), callcount (by number of calls, only for scoped cycle counters), num(by total inclusive time)
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]	- maxhistoryframes (default 60, number of frames used to generate the stats displayed on the hud)
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]	- reset (reset the accumulated history)
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]	- maxdepth (default 4, maximum depth for the hierarchy)
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat none - disables drawing all stats groups
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat group list|listall|enable name|disable name|none|all|default - manages stats groups
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat display -font=small[tiny]
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]	Changes stats rendering display options
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat startfile - starts dumping a capture
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat stopfile - stops dumping a capture (regular, raw, memory)
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat startfileraw - starts dumping a raw capture
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat toggledebug - toggles tracking the most memory expensive stats
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat slow [-ms=1.0] [-depth=4] - toggles displaying the game and render thread stats
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]add -memoryprofiler in the command line to enable the memory profiling
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat stopfile - stops tracking all memory operations and writes the results to the file
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat namedmarker #markername# - adds a custom marker to the stats stream
[2025.11.12-19.26.58:997][395]stat testfile - loads the last saved capture and dumps first, middle and last frame
